It also reports namespace declarations that contain a forbidden word as one of their segments, at any depth:

```php
namespace Evidence;

final class RunReader
{
}
```

```php
namespace App\Domain\Outcome;

final class PaymentReader
{
}
```

```php
namespace App\Probes\Http;

final class LatencyReader
{
}
```

### Not Reported

- Namespaces that only share a partial prefix, such as `Tests\Supporting`
- Namespaces outside the configured prefixes
- Segments that only contain a forbidden word, such as `App\EvidenceStore`
- Segments that differ in case, such as `App\evidence`
- The global namespace

## Matching Rules

Matching is case-sensitive. A namespace is reported only when it is an exact match or a child namespace.

